"""hand-gesture: webcam hand gestures drive Hyprland workspaces and windows (HANDGESTURE).

An open palm held for half a second arms the clutch. While armed, a vertical swipe cycles the focused
monitor's local workspaces (swipe up = next, swipe down = previous). A closed fist held for 0.6 s disarms.
There is no horizontal swipe action. Frames stay in memory; nothing is written to disk and nothing leaves the machine.

Phase 2 (only while armed): a one-hand pinch (thumb tip to index tip) held 0.12 s drags the focused window (pixels when
floating, move-direction steps when tiled); a two-hand pinch resizes it; a held Victory sign toggles fullscreen.
Swipes are suppressed while any pinch is active. HAND_GESTURE_DRYRUN=1 logs Hyprland dispatches instead of running them.

Usage:
  hand-gesture run                  daemon (hand-gesture.service)
  hand-gesture toggle               start or stop hand-gesture.service
  hand-gesture --probe --seconds N  print "frames=N hands=N ms_p50=X luma=Y" and exit (2 if no camera)

HUD state is published atomically to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hand-gesture/state.json (see StateWriter).
Optional config: ~/.config/hand-gesture/config.json (invert_vertical, swipe_dist, swipe_window_s, arm_hold_s,
mirror_x, drag_enabled, resize_enabled, fullscreen_enabled, pinch_on, pinch_off).
"""
